1. click() - used to click on element
2. clear() - used to clear existing / entered value in a field/textbox/text area
3. sendKeys(String valueToBeEntered) - used to enter value into field/textbox/text area
4. getText() - Used to fetch text from web element
5. getAttribute() - Used to fetch value present in a particular attribute
6. getDomAttribute() - in future
7. getProperty() - in future
7. getCssValue() - Used Whenever we want do a cosmetic validation (Look of the UI)
8. isEnabled() - checks if element is enambled (if enabled returns true, else false) ideally used for <button>, <input>, <select>, <textarea>
9. isSelected()
10. isDisplayed() - Verifies if an element is displayed on UI
11. getSize() - To verify height & width of element
12. getLocation() - to verify Allignment of element
13. getRect() - to verify both height, width & Allignment
14. getTagName() - Returns the tag name of the element in String format
15. submit() - it is used to click on buttons which comes under <form> tag

---------------Difference Between-----------------
16. findElement() - Is used to handle single element. Returns WebElement type Object
17. findElements() - Is used to handle Multiple Elements. Returns List<WebElement> type Object